# UML-only add-on to .kunitconfig.
#
# UML disables IOMEM by default (CONFIG_NO_IOMEM=y), which makes
# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT unreachable and with it the whole of sound/usb. The only
# user-selectable way in is UML_PCI_OVER_VIRTIO, which selects UML_PCI, which
# selects UML_IOMEM_EMULATION and hence INDIRECT_IOMEM; that in turn forces
# NO_IOMEM off and HAS_IOMEM on. VIRTIO_UML is a hard dependency of it.
#
# These symbols do not exist outside arch/um, and kunit.py treats any
# requested option that fails to appear in the generated .config as an error,
# so they cannot live in the main .kunitconfig. Use both fragments for UML:
#
#     kunit.py run --kunitconfig=sound/usb/jockey3 \
#                  --kunitconfig=sound/usb/jockey3/.kunitconfig.um
#
# tests/run_kunit.sh does this automatically for the "um" target.

CONFIG_VIRTIO=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_UML=y
CONFIG_UML_PCI_OVER_VIRTIO=y
CONFIG_UML_PCI_OVER_VIRTIO_DEVICE_ID=1
